  "description": "Message bodies (SPEC §4). defaults gives each type's default TTL in seconds and whether a payload-level reply_to is required (a missing one is bad_payload, SPEC §3.3 rule 5). collapse_cases gives the collapse real key for a body, or null when the type does not collapse. valid payloads MUST be accepted and parsed, including every V2 field of notification.posted@1. invalid_bodies MUST be rejected as bad_payload. missing_reply_to payloads have a valid body but lack the required reply_to. Integers marked int32 in SPEC §4 are signed 32-bit, so ARGB colours with the alpha bit set are negative. Blob references are the ones sealed in blob.json. The first valid payload and the inline reply, media state and seek command are also sealed in envelope_seal.json.",
